Date sent:  28-APR-1996 11:37:05 


I asked

>I'm attempting to set up an HJLJ4MPlus, using a JetDirect J2552A interface.  I
>have found several printcap and bootp entries in the list archives, and have 
>reached the point where it will print text, but not postscript, whether I use 
>autosensing or not.

>Text prints fine; PS files disappear from the queue, but nothing prints.

>The frustrating thing is that it works fine (autosensing and all) from a VMS 
>system!

I had many replies: most pointed out that text will print with rp=text; 
postscript requires rp=raw.

So, despite a message in the archives, I needed to set up two queues:

lp0|laser|hp4M:\
	:af=/usr/adm/lpacct:\
	:if=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
	:ct=network:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
	:lp=:\
	:of=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
	:rm=laser:\
	:rp=raw:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd:\
	:sh:
lp1|text:\
	:af=/usr/adm/lpacct:\
	:ct=network:\
	:lf=/usr/adm/lperr:\
	:lp=:\
	:rm=laser:\
	:rp=text:\
	:sd=/usr/spool/lpd:\
	:sh:

This seems to work fine.

Incidental comments I received included:

 - autosensing only works on VMS with a suitably long pause between different 
types of job 
 - the VMS queue is a Multinet Stream queue; the rules are different for LPQ 
   queues
 - the if and of parameters may not be effective for remote printers until
   dUnix version 3 (I'm running 3.2C) 

If anyone wants copies of the replies please email me.

