Apparently many of you running Digital UNIX already know about
this problem and just live with it.  I should have mentioned that
the idle time I was referring to is that which is displayed by
the finger and w commands.  I believe these commands actually 
read the idle time from the /var/adm/utmp file.

The Digital support person I was dealing with said that she
has submitted this to engineering (as a result of investigating
the problem for me).  However, I find it difficult to believe
this is the first time Digital has heard of the bug.  Mike
Crider specifically mentions the bug on his idled home page:
     www.cs.hope.edu/~crider/idled

