Too many people to mention told me to tun disklabel and provide a 'generic' 
disk type, basically telling disklabel to create it's own entry. This 
came about in DUX 3.0 and apparently most if not all 'newer' drives will 
accomodate this.
  The line I used was:

	# disklabel -rw rzx ST32550N

