From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Apr 16 11:32:48 1996
From: PASTORE () TRIESTE ! INFN ! IT
Date: Tue, 16 Apr 1996 11:32:48 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: how to stop POLYCENTER Security Intrusion detector.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076331021312

I have asked how to stop the id_mond process since 
neither "id_mond -k" nor kill -9 id_mond.pid was
enough.

The solution is simple:

SID creates an entry in the /etc/inittab file to make 
init respawning the process if it dies. It is enough
to change the action from respawn into off in the 
corresponding line of inittab. After kill -1 1 SID is 
definitely  stopped.

Thanks to Chua Koon Teck and to Krzysztof Palacz for the 
very quick answer!

