The problem is solved! Peter Stern <peter@wiscpa.weizmann.ac.il>
sent me the following solution - thanks a lot, Peter:

> Hi!
> We've bought a used DEClaser printer, unfortunately without a manual.
> It is configured for DEC PPL3 mode, but I'd like to switch to PostScript
> and hook it to our D.U. system. How do I switch to PS? I've tried pressing
> the different switches while turning it on, but so far no luck. Thought I
> should try here. Any ideas?
> Cheers,
> Terje Sten

Dear Terje:

I have this printer.  Here are the instructions:

   Operation                                           Display Reads
   ---------                                           -------------
1. Press On Line to place the printer offline.         00 READY DEC
2. Press and hold Menu for at least three seconds.     MODE = DEC
3. Press > once.                                       MODE  AdobePS
4. Press Enter to select the PostScript mode of        The printer recycles
   operation.                                          ...eventually:
                                                       PS READY/IDLE

To go back, you go off line and use the Menu to get into CONTROLLER MODE
and use > to get to MODE: DEC PPL3 and Enter (in brief).

Thanks to:
From: "Gernot M. Fuchs" <gfuchs@golay.med.unc.edu>
From: "Rainer Landes" <rlandes@fphws01.physik.uni-karlsruhe.de>
From: Hellebo Knut <Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com>
as well. One of those who replied tried to test the same as I, and so of course
got exactly the same problem ;) Anyway, the answer from Peter should bail
us all out for now!

Cheers,
Terje Sten


