Thanks goes to Dr. Blinn at Digital for his response.
    "Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-881-0646" <tpb@zk3.dec.com>

>>     I'm trying to setup up SLIP to go at 57600, but slattach won't accept
>>     anything higher than 38400.  I'm told the hardware is able support the
>>     57600 speed.  Is this a limitation for slattach or is there a work
>>      around that I'm not aware of?
     
>What version of Digital UNIX?  Prior to V3.2D, there was no support for
>the 57.6K speed in Digital UNIX.  With V3.2D, support was added.  If
>you're on an earlier version, you need to upgrade.  And I can't tell you
>for certain that in V3.2D the slattach utility got upgraded to support
>57.6K, there are a lot of things that did get updated, but we may have
>overlooked a few.
     
>The good news is that V4.0 will be shipping soon, and it should have both
>the 57.6K support and PPP support (which you should find better than
>slip).
     
>Tom
     

