     My original request is at the bottom of this message.
     
     Here is one particularly interresting answer from Selden E. Ball, Jr. 
     where he suggest upgrading to 3.2d instead of 3.2c. 
     ==================================================
     Jocelyn,
     
     In order to have reliable support for the DE500 10/100 e'net 
     interface, you need to upgrade your system's firmware to the most 
     recent version (at least to what is shipped on firmware CD V3.4) 
     and you need to upgrade Digital Unix to V3.2D.
     
     The two most recent versions of the firmware (as on Firmware CD V3.4 
     and V3.5) recognize Digital's 10/100 PCI ethernet chip and show the 
     vendor name.
     
     DU V3.2D includes patches for framing errors seen in V3.2C when one 
     uses a DE500 at high througput.
     
