Subject: RE: problems with SEAGATE disk installation on ALPHA station

     Eugene,
     
     You might want to try:
     
     # disklabel -z /dev/rrz1c
     
     to zero out the disklabel and then do:
     
     # disklabel -rw /dev/rrz1c RZxx
     
     In order to write the label onto the physical disk (-r option), the 
     disk label section has to be made writable first.  This is only done 
     through the -z and -e flags, which set a writable bit on the disk 
     itself.  After writing out the primary label with -rw, you can do an 
     -re to edit the layout directly.  I did this for a few of my disks 
     rather than trying to set up custom disktab entries.
     
     Bob Capps
     Perot Systems
